{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>An inheritance gained hurriedly at the beginning</b> — from robbery." "<b>but its end</b> — since it is stolen, it will not be blessed. The meaning: the rains of blessing will not descend upon it. And it is written מבוחלת with a chet, to indicate that a stolen inheritance is detestable and abominable to HaShem, from the root בחלה (to loathe)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The phrase 'the rains of blessing will not descend upon it' is a literal rendering; Ibn Ezra plays on the double meaning of ברכה as both 'blessing' and 'pooling/collecting' of rainwater."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:52.266412901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}